Greg,
I wanted to say thanks for your site and the many guitar tabs I have
found in it.  I have gotten a lot of lyrics for my own use and wanted to
give some feedback on those that I have found with errors and perhaps
some new additions in the future.
I play in a small C&W band here in Montana and I just finished
transcribing Trace Adkins' "Every Light In The House Is On" and when I
saw it in your files I noticed many differences from what I had done.
We each hear different things in a song so here is my rendition.  I have
included timing strokes that correspond to the 4/4 time it is written in
so the players will know where the beats are in relation to the words
and where the chord changes take place.  Just a note about the chorus,
towards the end trace walks down from a Bb to a G and then ends the last
line. If you have heard the song it will be easier to figure out but the
notes are Bb-A-G.  This is a lovely song and I hope everyone out there
enjoys it as much as I do.

EVERY LIGHT IN THE HOUSE IS ON
Trace Adkins

